Feature: a markdown doc cannot ship the same prose paragraph twice

  830 KB of one repeated paragraph sat in the project's reference
  specification for three days and eleven documenter commits before a human
  noticed. Nothing in the repo lints prose.

  This gate exits non-zero when a prose line repeats inside one markdown
  file. Markdown that is supposed to repeat — fences, rules, table
  separators, list markers, diagram glyphs — never trips it.

  Background:
    Given the documenter's doc-duplication gate

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-01
  Scenario: a document with no repeated prose passes
    Given a markdown file whose prose lines are all distinct
    When the gate runs on it
    Then the gate passes

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-02
  Scenario Outline: a repeated prose line fails the gate, and the report names what to fix
    Given a markdown file with one prose line appearing <count> times
    When the gate runs on it
    Then the gate fails
    And the report names the file, the repeated text, <count> occurrences, and the line numbers

    Examples:
      | count |
      | 2     |
      | 286   |

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-03
  Scenario Outline: markdown that is supposed to repeat never trips the gate
    Given a markdown file repeating only the structural line <line>
    When the gate runs on it
    Then the gate passes

    Examples:
      | line               |
      | code fence         |
      | horizontal rule    |
      | table separator    |
      | list marker        |
      | blockquote marker  |
      | diagram glyph      |

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-04
  Scenario: repetition across two files is not a duplicate
    Given two markdown files sharing one prose line
    When the gate runs on both
    Then the gate passes

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-05
  Scenario: every named file is checked, not just the first
    Given a clean markdown file and a markdown file with a repeated prose line
    When the gate runs on both
    Then the gate fails
    And the report names the second file

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-06
  Scenario: the repaired reference specification passes
    Given the specification after its duplicate paragraphs are removed
    When the gate runs on it
    Then the gate passes

  # BL-693 doc-dup-gate-07
  Scenario: the corrupted reference specification fails
    Given the specification while it still holds 286 copies of one paragraph
    When the gate runs on it
    Then the gate fails
